  "finding": "Iron Beetle retains its mandibles, lower head plate, horns, segmented underside and shell profile across source and battle clip phases. Personally inspected all eight original raw sheets and eight exposure diagnostic copies because dark materials conceal small joint details; fresh opposite and underside views confirm connected lower head and leg roots without a torn underside. All six segmented legs track the shell during jump, strike, fall, revive and recovery rather than remaining behind. The24 advancing-idle frames,216 actual companion technique frames and16 atlas cells were personally inspected; no deformation repair identified. Diagnostic lighting clips bright claw reflections, so claw geometry was also checked in production runtime and technique views.",
